# Paired Route: Herbalism + Alchemy 1-300 (WoW: Forever 1.60.1 only)
# Follows docs/MULTI_PROFESSION_RULES.md:
# - Dedicated per-combination file: guides/pairs/herbalism-alchemy.guide
# - Single-anchor sections on Alchemy (the crafting anchor) in rising order,
#   so Polestar's section auto-skip and remaining-material subtraction work;
#   Herbalism trains and skill checkpoints are interleaved inside each
#   Alchemy bracket.
# - Every `collect ... gather Herbalism <rank>` (and the Fishing oil
#   reagents) has a matching `auction` goal in the same section so Mix /
#   Gather / Buy modes all work cleanly.
# - Alchemy crafts, vendor goods and material counts follow the solo
#   guides/alchemy.guide route; Herbalism trainers and herb loops follow
#   guides/herbalism.guide. Ids and coordinates were resolved from the
#   Forever client data (build 1.60.1) for those solo guides.
#
# Herbalism checkpoints, mapped onto the Alchemy brackets:
#   Alchemy   1-55   -> Herbalism  70   (starter herbs)
#   Alchemy  55-90   -> Herbalism 100   (Mageroyal, Earthroot)
#   Alchemy  90-130  -> Herbalism 150   (Briarthorn, Stranglekelp, Kingsblood)
#   Alchemy 130-195  -> Herbalism 200   (Kingsblood, Stranglekelp, Liferoot)
#   Alchemy 195-225  -> Herbalism 230   (Liferoot, Sungrass unlocked)
#   Alchemy 225-250  -> Herbalism 250   (Blindweed needs 235; Hinterlands loop)
#   Alchemy 265-300  -> Herbalism 300   (Sungrass and the Felwood herbs)
#
# Forever Scarce herbs are uncommon bonus drops from ordinary herb nodes,
# not dedicated nodes. This route is the whole point of the pair: you pick
# them while you gather for the current brew band.
#   Frilled Lichen  -> Cerulean Dye   (Alchemy 50)
#   Rosecap         -> Magenta Dye    (Alchemy 130)
#   Stranglevine    -> Viridian Dye   (Alchemy 230)
#   Pyrite (Mining) -> Sulfuric Acid  (Alchemy 50; buy on the Auction House
#                      if you do not mine)

guide forever-professions/pair-herbalism-alchemy
title Herbalism + Alchemy 1-300
category Professions
folder Paired Routes
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Azeroth
keywords herbalism, alchemy, paired, dyes, scarce
pitch Level Herbalism and Alchemy together from 1 to 300: pick the herbs for your current brew band and hoard the Scarce bonus drops that become dyes.
pro Every herb on the Alchemy route is picked by you, so the Auction House only covers the gaps
pro Frilled Lichen, Rosecap and Stranglevine turn into Cerulean, Magenta and Viridian Dye, which Tailoring and other crafters pay well for
pro Both professions give Legacy Points from the crafting side, and the Alchemy Mana Well camp feature comes with the route
con Uses both primary profession slots, so you carry no other profession until you swap
con Herb nodes are shared with other gatherers, so a busy realm slows the picking bands

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

section Alchemy 1-55

step Learn Herbalism
  only Alliance
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Herbalism takes one of your two primary slots and Alchemy takes the other. Nancy Songflower in Elwynn Forest teaches Apprentice Herbalism at any character level. Turn on Find Herbs from the Herbalism box of the Professions window and drag it to your action bar: it switches off every time you die, and it replaces Find Minerals while it is on.
  train Herbalism Apprentice npc 247223

step Learn Herbalism
  only Horde
  zone Durotar
  tip Herbalism takes one of your two primary slots and Alchemy takes the other. Zor'la in the Valley of Trials teaches Apprentice Herbalism at any character level. Turn on Find Herbs from the Herbalism box of the Professions window and drag it to your action bar: it switches off every time you die, and it replaces Find Minerals while it is on.
  train Herbalism Apprentice npc 267329

step Starter Herbs to 70 (Elwynn Forest)
  only Alliance
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Pick every Peacebloom, Silverleaf and Earthroot (Earthroot needs skill 15) and circle the waypoints to Herbalism 70. Forever's starting areas also grow Wilted Peacebloom and Stunted Silverleaf, pickable from skill 1. Keep every herb: your first brews need 54 Silverleaf and 45 Peacebloom. If a Frilled Lichen drops as a bonus, keep it: it becomes Cerulean Dye at Alchemy 50.
  goto 53.0,38.0 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 52.6,42.1 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 56.9,43.0 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 47.6,47.5 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 47.7,37.8 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 50.8,83.4 "Earthroot" r 30
  goto 78.5,76.4 "Silverleaf, Peacebloom" r 30
  skill Herbalism 70

step Starter Herbs to 70 (Durotar)
  only Horde
  zone Durotar
  tip Pick every Peacebloom, Silverleaf and Earthroot (Earthroot needs skill 15) and circle the waypoints to Herbalism 70. Forever's starting areas also grow Wilted Peacebloom and Stunted Silverleaf, pickable from skill 1. Keep every herb: your first brews need 54 Silverleaf and 45 Peacebloom. If a Frilled Lichen drops as a bonus, keep it: it becomes Cerulean Dye at Alchemy 50.
  goto 42.2,62.6 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 46.2,62.7 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 46.5,58.3 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 43.6,66.8 "Wilted Peacebloom, Stunted Silverleaf" r 30
  goto 52.3,57.9 "Silverleaf, Peacebloom" r 30
  goto 36.8,28.4 "Peacebloom, Earthroot" r 30
  goto 57.1,22.4 "Silverleaf, Peacebloom" r 30
  skill Herbalism 70

step Learn Alchemy
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Vosur Brakthel in Tinker Town, Ironforge, teaches Apprentice Alchemy at any character level. With your herbs already in the bags, your first brews are free of Auction House trips.
  train Alchemy Apprentice npc 1246

step Learn Alchemy
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Whuut in Orgrimmar teaches Apprentice Alchemy at any character level. With your herbs already in the bags, your first brews are free of Auction House trips.
  train Alchemy Apprentice npc 11046

step Alchemy 1-55: Auction House
  tip What the first elixirs take that the Auction House sells: 54 Silverleaf, 45 Peacebloom. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 765 x54
  auction 2447 x45

step Alchemy 1-55: herbs
  tip Silverleaf and Peacebloom are the starter herbs you just picked: take them from your bags or your bank.
  collect 765 x54 anywhere gather Herbalism 1
  collect 2447 x45 anywhere gather Herbalism 1

step Alchemy 1-55: vendor goods
  tip Empty Vials come from Alchemy supply vendors; most trainers have one nearby.
  buy 3371 x54 nearest

step Elixir of Minor Force, Elixir of Minor Defense (1-55)
  tip Elixir of Minor Force, 9 brews to 10, then Elixir of Minor Defense, 45 brews to 55: a Silverleaf and a Peacebloom in each of the second. Both are taught with Apprentice Alchemy. At Alchemy 50 you can also learn Cerulean Dye and Sulfuric Acid: save your Frilled Lichen, and buy Pyrite on the Auction House if you do not mine.
  learn 1245250 "Elixir of Minor Force"
  craft 1245250 "Elixir of Minor Force" until 10
  learn 7183 "Elixir of Minor Defense"
  craft 7183 "Elixir of Minor Defense" until 55

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman

section Alchemy 55-90

step Journeyman Herbalism
